# Lens

> From Kubernetes control to governed AI agents

Lens is a product family developed by Mirantis, Inc. The canonical product website is https://lenshq.io.

Lens builds tools for operating production infrastructure. Lens K8S IDE is the Kubernetes IDE used by over a million engineers; Lens Agents is a governed platform for running AI agents against enterprise systems. Both are built for environments where access, policy, and audit matter.

Last updated: 2026-08-13

## Key facts

- Over 1 million users, at companies including Microsoft, NVIDIA, Cisco, and Disney.
- Compliance: a SOC 2 Type 1 audit opinion covers Lens K8S IDE, and Mirantis Inc. holds ISO 27001. Lens Agents is built under that control framework but is not separately certified.
- Lens K8S IDE runs on macOS, Windows, and Linux. Free tier plus paid editions.
- Lens Agents is commercial and self-hosted: a Helm install into your own Kubernetes cluster, with no hosted control plane. There is no SaaS or marketplace option.
- Domains: lenshq.io is product and marketing, docs.k8slens.dev is documentation, app.k8slens.dev is sign-in.

