## Products

Lens K8S IDE and Lens Agents are peer products. Neither requires the other, and they do not share a control plane — they are separate products from the same company, for adjacent problems.

### Lens K8S IDE

**For:** Engineers, SREs, and platform teams who work with Kubernetes.

A desktop IDE for Kubernetes: connect clusters, inspect workloads, read logs and metrics, and operate day to day from one workspace.

- A standalone desktop application. No SaaS, no control plane, and nothing to install into your clusters.
- Connects with your existing kubeconfig and enforces Kubernetes RBAC exactly as configured — no admin service account, no privileged in-cluster agent.
- Scales from a single-node minikube to clusters with 1000+ nodes and hundreds of thousands of pods, without overloading the cluster or the machine it runs on.
- Multi-cluster access to any cluster with a Kubernetes API — managed cloud services (EKS, AKS, GKE), any on-premises distribution, and local clusters such as minikube or kind.
- Built-in GitOps: Flux integration, showing what is synced, failing, or drifting next to the live workloads.
- Workloads, events, logs, metrics, Helm releases, RBAC, and an integrated terminal in one view.
- Bring your own AI coding agent — Claude Code, Codex, GitHub Copilot CLI, or Gemini CLI — running inside Lens with full cluster context. No API key of your own required.
- A built-in MCP server, so external AI agents can work with your Kubernetes clusters through Lens — under the same kubeconfig and RBAC.
- Security Center and Teamwork in paid editions.

