## Frequently confused concepts

- Lens Agents is not an AI model or an AI assistant. It runs agents you already use — MCP clients like Claude Code, Claude Desktop, and Cursor, and long-running agents like OpenClaw and Hermes Agent — plus agents you supply as a container image.
- Lens Agents does not make an organization EU AI Act compliant. No product can. It supplies controls and evidence — agent identity, recorded actions, declared autonomy — that an organization uses to meet its own obligations.
- Lens does not publish a proprietary foundation model. You bring the model; Lens governs what the agent running on it can reach and do.
- Lens K8S IDE is not a SaaS dashboard. It is a desktop application that uses your kubeconfig, with nothing installed into your clusters.
- Lens Agents is not a hosted service. You install it into your own environment with Helm.

